        "response": {
          "output": "Add the Cinnamon agent to your build, then pick a backend and opt in the actors you want measured. It needs an Akka subscription and the commercial resolvers/credentials.\n\n**1. sbt setup** (Maven and Gradle have equivalents):\n```scala\n// project/plugins.sbt\naddSbtPlugin(\"com.lightbend.cinnamon\" % \"sbt-cinnamon\" % \"2.22.x\")\n\n// build.sbt\nenablePlugins(Cinnamon)\nrun / cinnamon := true\ntest / cinnamon := true\nlibraryDependencies ++= Seq(\n  Cinnamon.library.cinnamonAkka,           // required\n  Cinnamon.library.cinnamonPrometheus,     // a backend is required, or nothing is exported\n  // add the modules that match what you run:\n  Cinnamon.library.cinnamonAkkaTyped,\n  Cinnamon.library.cinnamonAkkaPersistence,\n  Cinnamon.library.cinnamonAkkaCluster,\n  Cinnamon.library.cinnamonAkkaStream\n)\n```\n\n**2. Opt in actors.** Actor telemetry is off by default. In `application.conf`:\n```hocon\ncinnamon.akka.actors { \"/user/*\" { report-by = class } }\n```\nGroup by class and pick specific paths. Instrumenting every actor causes a metric explosion.\n\n**3. Run it on every cluster node.** The agent attaches with `-javaagent`, and each node reports independently. In production, set the `-javaagent` flag yourself if you don't run through sbt.\n\n**4. Point your stack at it.** Use Prometheus with Grafana, or OpenTelemetry. Add the Jaeger or Zipkin reporter if you want traces across nodes.\n\nThe free [[akka-diagnostics]] covers startup config and starvation checks. It doesn't replace Insights.\n\nI took this from the toolkit's `akka-insights` skill, not from the live docs. Check the plugin version against https://doc.akka.io/libraries/akka-insights/current/. The `2.22.x` in the skill is a placeholder."
        },
